+# Generic ACP Guide fallback
+
+The generic ACP port has no negotiated, acknowledged vendor steering path. Its
+`deliverGuideAtToolBoundary` therefore returns `unavailable`, including during a
+Host approval wait. A local hold or one-way `session/steer` notification cannot
+prove acceptance, and this adapter sends neither.
+
+Core retains the original Guide input in its existing pending queue. After the
+current ACP prompt settles, the existing native continuation uses the same vendor
+session and sends that input once through ordinary `session/prompt`. Approval,
+denial, Stop and checkpoint behavior remain on their original paths; Guide does
+not resolve permission or restart an interrupted turn.
+
+Claude SDK and Codex app-server steering, and the global Host Guide admission gate,
+remain unchanged. No new vendor extension or public API is selected here. A future
+vendor-specific path requires advertised support and acceptance evidence before it
+can return vendor-delivered.
+
+Verification uses actual Core + ACP stdio + SQLite with an agent that advertises no
+steering and ignores unknown notifications. It proves no vendor-delivered marker,
+one later prompt in the original vendor session, preserved allow/deny, and no
+continuation or effects after Stop. Synthetic responses incur no paid inference.
