+## ZK-FIX receipt contract
+
+The existing Session store owns every receipt. A physical observation relating to
+several conversations has a distinct stable entry key in each Session; phase
+updates use that same key. Existing unscoped entries remain readable and are not
+migrated or reassigned. Legacy receipts without a phase are settled observations.
+Requested and unknown receipts never synthesize terminal linked-task events.
+
+An unknown or unsent Session is skipped without creating a record. One failed
+writer must not block another Session. Only an explicit durable acknowledgement
+counts as written; failure results retain the receipt identity and failed bindings
+for an explicit retry. A late acknowledgement cannot clear a newer binding.
+
+```text
+remote owner -> existing Session writer -> per-Session acknowledged result
+             -> failed/unknown result retains original identity
+controlled idle -> await requested receipt while proxy is live -> dispose proxy
+abrupt close -> unknown write outcome; captured proxy is not an offline store
+```
+
+Controlled idle disposal may journal a requested receipt before closing the proxy.
+It does not claim that a post-close proxy can persist a settled observation. There
+is no new outbox, retry runner, Session store, or permission path. Acceptance uses
+the public Client/Server with real local ports and SQLite, including cold reopen,
+drafts, independent failures, duplicates, late acknowledgements and legacy reads.
+
+The idle receipt acknowledgement has a finite 5-second default budget. Timeout or
+failure reports an unknown outcome and proceeds with teardown. The connection
+registry rechecks current ownership after that await; a newer logical owner or
+running task cancels the older idle disposal.
+
