index 00000000..93337249
--- /dev/null
+++ b/apps/zcode-cli/docs/session-shutdown-settlement.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Session shutdown settlement
+
+ZK-FIX/S repairs the existing Runtime, App, resident pool and CLI owners. It creates
+no new store, accepted queue, permission rule or public wire method.
+
+Admission fences synchronously before cancellation. Core retains each failed queued
+command under its original input ID and frozen intent; every waiting caller settles.
+A later close retries only remaining commands. Existing durable queue evidence is
+reconciled before publication, so a lost acknowledgement does not duplicate it.
+Cold reopen retains the existing discard policy and never runs preserved input.
+
+App close has a bounded acknowledgement and a separate actual settlement promise.
+Successful/pending owned resource closes are joined once; failed closes may retry in
+the same App. The resident pool retains the old record privately after registry
+removal and holds the reactivation gate through actual settlement. A failed gate
+refuses the current operation; the next operation retries the old owner before any
+new App can activate.
+
+Protocol cleanup observes one absolute finite cleanup grace, shared with the CLI's
+existing six-second close budget. The process watchdog adds only a bounded output
+flush allowance. Cleanup that cannot settle exits nonzero. EOF followed by successful
+settlement exits zero; a later failure can upgrade an initial EOF zero. Known receipt
+writers retain SQLite and dependencies during the grace; forced kill remains an
+unknown boundary and does not imply receipt durability.
+
+Verification uses public App/pool/Protocol paths, real SQLite, a real child process
+and controlled storage/resource failure. It checks original IDs and duplicate
+receipts, cold discard, a 2.2-second known receipt write, failed/retried cleanup,
+finite forced exit and the existing delayed factory/late effect tests. Test model
+responses are synthetic; paid inference, real UI acceptance and foreign process
+cleanup are separate evidence.
